; Move Willy by one pass: jump, fall, keys, walking, ramps, conveyors, walls
;
; Called once per pass of the frame loop #R$89AD (not in ending stage 3), after the entities have been
; moved and before Willy is drawn (#R$95C8). It changes only Willy's variables: Y #R$85CF, move state
; #R$85D0, air state #R$85D1, walk frame #R$85D2, attribute address #R$85D3, jump step #R$85D5 and, when
; he walks off the room, the room itself (the #R$948A routines never return). It is one long routine
; whose parts are reached by JP and fall-through; the entry points are labelled and could be split
; (see the comments at each label). Order of work in a pass:
; .
; 1. Rope. If #R$85D6 says Willy holds a rope (1-$80) the jump and ground code is skipped and the
; pass goes straight to the keys ($8ED4, which then skips the ground logic as well).
; .
; 2. Jump (air state 1, MoveWilly). The step counter #R$85D5 counts 0-17. In every pass Y changes by
; (step AND $FE) - 8 index units: -8 -8 -6 -6 -4 -4 -2 -2 0 0 +2 +2 +4 +4 +6 +6 +8 +8, so he rises 40 units
; (20 pixel rows, 2.5 character rows) in 8 passes, hangs for 3 and comes down again; at step 18 he is
; back at his take-off height and the state becomes 6 (a fall). If either of the two cells of his
; top row now holds the wall tile he bumps his head: Y becomes the row boundary below Y + 16 and a
; fall (state 2) starts. Walking goes on during the jump but the keys are not read again, so the direction at
; take-off cannot be changed. Each pass clicks the speaker (pitch follows the distance from the apex).
; The ground test is made only after steps 13 and 16, which is how Willy can land on a platform that
; is 2 or 1 character rows above his take-off floor; a platform 3 rows up cannot be landed on.
; .
; 3. Ground test (MoveWilly_Ground), for every state other than a jump in progress (and after jump
; steps 13 and 16): while Y is between two character rows there is no ground; otherwise the two
; cells below Willy's feet (two rows down from #R$85D3) are ground when neither holds the nasty tile
; and at least one is not background (any wall, floor, ramp or conveyor attribute counts; a nasty
; cell under his feet also kills him in #R$961E). Below the bottom of the room he leaves through
; #R$94D2.
; .
; 4. No ground (MoveWilly_Air). Walking is switched off (bit 1 of #R$85D0 cleared). State 0 becomes 2
; (a fall starts, nothing moves yet); in a fall the state counts up once per pass (2, 3, ... $0F, then
; back to $0C), Willy drops 8 index units (4 pixel rows) per pass and the speaker clicks with a falling
; pitch. Falling has no horizontal movement.
; .
; 5. Ground found (MoveWilly_Supported). A fall state of $0C or more kills Willy (#R$90B7). From
; standing at the top of a fall that means a drop of 5 character rows or more (4 rows is survived);
; after a jump that ended over a gap (state 6) a drop of 3 rows kills. The state becomes 0. Then
; the input is collected as one byte of key bits (bits 0, 2, 4 mean right, bits 1, 3, 5 mean left,
; 0 = pressed): the conveyor under his feet, the keys, the Kempston joystick (only if #R$85CE) and,
; in ending stages 2 and 3, a forced right key. Left keys: Q E T U O 5 6 and joystick left. Right
; keys: W R Y I P 7 8 and joystick right. Jump keys: CAPS SHIFT Z X C V B N M SYMBOL SHIFT SPACE, 0
; and joystick fire (ignored in ending stages 2 and 3). The key bits and the old move state
; select the new state in #R$8421 (both directions together, which includes a key held against a
; conveyor, leave the state unchanged). A jump key starts the jump (air state 1, step 0) and the
; pass goes on to the walking code, with the move state just computed.
; .
; 6. Walking (MoveWilly_Walk). Only if bit 1 of #R$85D0 is set and no rope is held. Willy takes one
; cell (8 pixels) every 4 passes: the frame #R$85D2 counts 3 down to 0 when facing left and 0 up to 3
; when facing right, and the step is taken in the pass that finds the frame at the end of its count
; (the frame is then reset). On the ground the step follows a ramp: a ramp cell next to his feet (the
; cell depends on the ramp direction #R$80DA) moves Willy one row up or down together with the
; sideways step. The cells he steps into must not hold the wall tile: the cell beside his lower row
; (and beside a third row while he straddles three rows in a jump), for a step right also the cell
; beside his head row. A step left from column 0 or a step right from column 30 leaves the room
; through #R$948A or #R$949E.
; .
; Quirk (observed): a step to the right also tests the cell at his head level, a step to the left
; does not, so a wall cell that is only at head height blocks him when he walks right but not when
; he walks left.
; .
; Hardware: reads the keyboard half rows with IN (ports $DFFE, $FBFE, $E7FE, $EFFE, $7EFE), the
; Kempston port $1F when #R$85CE is set, and writes port $FE (speaker bits and the room's border
; colour) for the jump and fall clicks.
@label=MoveWilly
c$8DD3 LD A,($85D6)  ; rope variable
 $8DD6 DEC A         ; bit 7 clear only for 1-$80: a rope is held
 $8DD7 BIT 7,A       ;
 $8DD9 JP Z,$8ED4    ; holding a rope: read the keys, no jump or fall
 $8DDC LD A,($85D1)  ; air state
@isub=CP AIR_JUMPING
 $8DDF CP $01        ;
 $8DE1 JR NZ,$8E36   ; not in a jump: ground test
 $8DE3 LD A,($85D5)  ; jump step
 $8DE6 AND $FE       ; steps 2n and 2n+1 give the same change
@isub=SUB JUMP_APEX_STEP
 $8DE8 SUB $08       ; -8 at the start, 0 at the apex, +8 at the end
 $8DEA LD HL,$85CF   ; Y index
 $8DED ADD A,(HL)    ;
 $8DEE LD (HL),A     ; Y after the rise or fall of the jump
@isub=CP Y_WRAPPED_MIN
 $8DEF CP $F0        ;
 $8DF1 JP NC,$94B0   ; Y wrapped below 0: through the top of the room
 $8DF4 CALL $8E9C    ; new attribute address; HL = top-left cell
 $8DF7 LD A,($80B2)  ; wall attribute: is his head in a wall?
 $8DFA CP (HL)       ;
 $8DFB JP Z,$8EBC    ; left cell of the top row: head bump
 $8DFE INC HL        ;
 $8DFF CP (HL)       ;
 $8E00 JP Z,$8EBC    ; right cell of the top row: head bump
 $8E03 LD A,($85D5)  ; no bump: next jump step
 $8E06 INC A         ;
 $8E07 LD ($85D5),A  ;
@isub=SUB JUMP_APEX_STEP
 $8E0A SUB $08       ; click delay from the distance to the apex
 $8E0C JP P,$8E11    ;
 $8E0F NEG           ; absolute value
*$8E11 INC A         ; delay = (distance + 1) * 8
 $8E12 RLCA          ;
 $8E13 RLCA          ;
 $8E14 RLCA          ;
 $8E15 LD D,A        ;
@isub=LD C,STEP_SOUND_TOGGLES
 $8E16 LD C,$20      ;
 $8E18 LD A,($80DE)  ; border colour of the room
@isub=OUT (ULA_PORT),A
*$8E1B OUT ($FE),A   ; click: speaker bits and border
@isub=XOR BEEPER_BITS
 $8E1D XOR $18       ;
 $8E1F LD B,D        ;
*$8E20 DJNZ $8E20    ;
 $8E22 DEC C         ;
 $8E23 JR NZ,$8E1B   ;
 $8E25 LD A,($85D5)  ; jump step after this pass
@isub=CP JUMP_END_STEP
 $8E28 CP $12        ;
 $8E2A JP Z,$8EB0    ; step 18: the jump is over, fall
@isub=CP JUMP_LAND_SECOND
 $8E2D CP $10        ;
 $8E2F JR Z,$8E36    ; step 16: test for ground
@isub=CP JUMP_LAND_FIRST
 $8E31 CP $0D        ;
 $8E33 JP NZ,$8FBC   ; other steps: skip the ground test and walk
; Ground test: is there something to stand on? (reached from #R$8DD3 for every air state but a jump
; in progress, and falls through from the jump steps 13 and 16). While Y is between two character
; rows there is no ground. The jump code falls into this part.
@label=MoveWilly_Ground
*$8E36 LD A,($85CF)  ; Y index
@isub=AND Y_BETWEEN_MASK
 $8E39 AND $0E       ; Y between two character rows?
 $8E3B JR NZ,$8E62   ; yes: no ground
 $8E3D LD HL,($85D3) ; attribute address of the top-left cell
@isub=LD DE,2*SCREEN_COLS
 $8E40 LD DE,$0040   ; two rows down: the cells under his feet
 $8E43 ADD HL,DE     ;
 $8E44 BIT 1,H       ; $5E00 or more: below the room
 $8E46 JP NZ,$94D2   ; falls out of the bottom of the room
 $8E49 LD A,($80BB)  ; nasty attribute: not ground
 $8E4C CP (HL)       ;
 $8E4D JR Z,$8E62    ; nasty under the left foot: no ground
 $8E4F INC HL        ;
 $8E50 LD A,($80BB)  ;
 $8E53 CP (HL)       ;
 $8E54 JR Z,$8E62    ; nasty under the right foot: no ground
 $8E56 LD A,($80A0)  ; background attribute
 $8E59 CP (HL)       ; right cell
 $8E5A DEC HL        ;
 $8E5B JP NZ,$8ED4   ; right cell is not background: ground
 $8E5E CP (HL)       ; left cell
 $8E5F JP NZ,$8ED4   ; left cell is not background: ground
; No ground under Willy (or a jump between its ground tests): continue the jump walking, or start or
; continue a fall.
@label=MoveWilly_Air
*$8E62 LD A,($85D1)  ; air state
@isub=CP AIR_JUMPING
 $8E65 CP $01        ;
 $8E67 JP Z,$8FBC    ; jumping: walk
 $8E6A LD HL,$85D0   ; move state
@isub=RES MOVE_WALK_BIT,(HL)
 $8E6D RES 1,(HL)    ; no walking in a fall
 $8E6F LD A,($85D1)  ;
 $8E72 OR A          ;
 $8E73 JP Z,$8EB6    ; was on the ground: start falling, nothing moves yet
 $8E76 INC A         ; next fall state
@isub=CP AIR_FALL_WRAP
 $8E77 CP $10        ;
 $8E79 JR NZ,$8E7D   ;
@isub=LD A,AIR_FATAL_FALL
 $8E7B LD A,$0C      ; states cycle 12-15 in a long fall
@label=MoveWilly_Fall
*$8E7D LD ($85D1),A  ; store the fall state
 $8E80 RLCA          ;
 $8E81 RLCA          ;
 $8E82 RLCA          ;
 $8E83 RLCA          ; click delay = state * 16: lower pitch the longer he falls
 $8E84 LD D,A        ;
@isub=LD C,STEP_SOUND_TOGGLES
 $8E85 LD C,$20      ;
 $8E87 LD A,($80DE)  ; border colour of the room
@isub=OUT (ULA_PORT),A
*$8E8A OUT ($FE),A   ;
@isub=XOR BEEPER_BITS
 $8E8C XOR $18       ;
 $8E8E LD B,D        ;
*$8E8F DJNZ $8E8F    ;
 $8E91 DEC C         ;
 $8E92 JR NZ,$8E8A   ;
 $8E94 LD A,($85CF)  ; Y index
@isub=ADD A,Y_FALL_STEP
 $8E97 ADD A,$08     ; 4 pixel rows down per pass
 $8E99 LD ($85CF),A  ; and fall into SetWillyCell
